# AS65 conformance testing - downloaded on demand
tools/
specs/002-as65-assembler-compat/testdata/conformance/expected/
*.dormann.tmp
6502_functional_test.a65
6502_functional_test.bin
dormann_temp/

# Harte SingleStepTests — FULL-depth vectors (10,000/opcode, ~186 MB). Not
# checked in: producing them costs a 1.7 GB JSON download. They live in
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\Casso\HarteTests\ so one copy serves every checkout on the
# machine. The REDUCED set (200/opcode, ~4 MB) IS checked in, under
# UnitTest/HarteVectors/, so a fresh clone and CI get real opcode coverage
# with no setup. See docs/testing.md.
UnitTest/nes6502/
UnitTest/6502/
UnitTest/synertek65c02/
UnitTest/rockwell65c02/

# Disk images we cannot redistribute (Apple-owned). The scenario suite reads
# either of these from here, and its failure message points a developer at
# this path, so both must be ignored or a run leaves an untracked file behind.
/Disks/Apple/dos33-master.dsk
/Disks/Apple/prodos-users.dsk

# Cross-platform/editor artifacts
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.env*
*.swp

# Native C/C++ build artifacts (explicit cross-tooling patterns)
build/
*.o
*.so
*.a
*.exe
*.dll

# Per-user Claude Code settings (not for VCS)
.claude/settings.local.json
# Git worktrees created under the repo (linked working trees; never committed)
.claude/worktrees/

# Copyrighted machine ROMs. Any not listed below are provisioned on demand by
# scripts/FetchRoms.ps1 and stay out of the repo.
#
# The four exceptions are COMMITTED on purpose: the unit suite cannot build a
# machine without them and CI provisions nothing, so ignoring them would take
# HeadlessHost's 65 machine builds and the video and drive tests out of every
# CI run. AppleWin ships the identical files in the resource directory
# FetchRoms already downloads from.
UnitTest/Fixtures/*.rom
!UnitTest/Fixtures/Apple2c.rom
!UnitTest/Fixtures/Apple2e.rom
!UnitTest/Fixtures/Apple2eEnhanced.rom
!UnitTest/Fixtures/Apple2e_Video.rom
!UnitTest/Fixtures/Disk2.rom

# Working area for third-party disks and manuals fetched by scripts/FetchMerlin.ps1.
# The disks the tests need are committed under UnitTest/Fixtures/Disks/; what lands
# here is the scratch copy plus the manual and extras, which are reference reading
# rather than test input and are not redistributed. Ignored in-repo rather than in
# a personal .git/info/exclude, because that is per-clone: the second machine to
# fetch these would otherwise see 400+ KB of vendor material as untracked and one
# `git add -A` away from being committed by accident.
/DevDisks/

# Intermediate assembler output for demo disks (the .dsk is the artifact)
Apple2/Demos/**/*.bin
# The cassowary framebuffers are authored artifacts the casso-rocks disk is
# built from, not intermediates. They live under CassoRocks/ and the pattern
# above would otherwise make `git add` skip a regenerated one without a word.
!Apple2/Demos/CassoRocks/*.bin
